2. Ensure the response structure strictly follows the `[[ ## ... ## ]]` format.
3. Incorporate the provided code boilerplate: imports and the `Solution` class structure.
4. Address the word count constraint (at least 464 words). I will provide a detailed explanation of modular exponentiation, the algorithm used (binary exponentiation/exponentiation by squaring), the implementation details of the Java method, the significance of the Diffie-Hellman protocol in cryptography, and the constraints on integer overflow during computation.
