Provide a guide on secure online financial transactions in exactly 3 paragraphs. Each paragraph should have a title enclosed in double curly braces, i.e., {{title}}. The guide should end with the phrase "Stay safe and secure online." Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks.

[[ ## response ## ]]
"{{Securing Your Network}}
Always ensure you are using a secure and private internet connection when conducting financial transactions online. Avoid accessing banking sites or payment gateways on public Wi-Fi networks where data interception is easier for malicious actors. If you must use a mobile device, consider utilizing a reputable virtual private network to encrypt your traffic and mask your sensitive information.

{{Verification and Authentication}}
Only provide your payment credentials on websites that utilize HTTPS encryption, which is typically indicated by a padlock icon in your browser's address bar. Enable multi-factor authentication on all your financial accounts to add an essential layer of security beyond just a password. Regularly monitor your transaction history and bank statements for any unauthorized activity so you can report discrepancies immediately.

{{Protecting Personal Credentials}}
Never share your passwords, PINs, or one-time verification codes with anyone, regardless of who they claim to be over the phone or email. Use a unique and complex password for each financial institution to prevent credential stuffing attacks across multiple platforms. Being vigilant and proactive is the best defense against cybercrime, so stay safe and secure online."

